<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch07-partial-derivatives-jacobian" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Partial Derivatives, Differentials, and the Jacobian Matrix</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Partial derivatives use ordinary derivatives along coordinate slices. Directional derivatives, the gradient, and the total derivative then describe change in all input directions. We distinguish the existence of partial derivatives from a valid linear approximation, and organize vector-valued derivatives into Jacobian matrices.</p>
  </introduction>

